{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EDvshvnALmuuoxM7AhVL5L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: \"将 'capability trap' 从 'structural inevitability' 弱化为 'primary contributing factor alongside fine-tuning regime'。两个 failure mechanisms (degeneracy + LP compression) 仍完全成立——它们的证据全部来自已完成实验，不受新实验影响。调整 claims 强度：'universally fail' → 'predominantly fail across tested configurations'。LoRA ablation 变为 nuanced finding：'output convergence is driven by capability AND fine-tuning intensity, with capability as the dominant factor.' 将 QE evaluation framework (Claim 2) 提升为 co-primary contribution。标题微调为 'Strong Predictors, Weak Selectors: Diagnosing Why...' 强调诊断而非绝对性。目标：EMNLP Main（adjusted claims）或 strong Findings。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"fewnerd_smoke\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: \"Few-NERD INTRA coarse 8-type, 1-epoch LoRA fine-tune + 200-instance N=8 pilot. Gate for full run.\"\n    expected_results:\n      train_loss_1epoch: 0.15\n      eval_loss_1epoch: 0.12\n      greedy_f1_200inst: 0.78\n      parse_rate: 0.998\n      pilot_sj_rho_full: 0.30\n      pilot_degeneracy_rate: 0.22\n      pilot_oracle_f1: 0.86\n      pilot_headroom_pp: 8.0\n      inference_time_200inst_minutes: 12\n      n_entity_types: 8\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 8.5\n    result_rationale: \"Few-NERD INTRA coarse（8类通用实体：Person, Organization, Location, Building, Product, Event, Art, Other）比 SciERC 更标准化但比 CoNLL 更细粒度。1-epoch LoRA 已足够让 Qwen3-8B 学会格式和基本类型映射（类似 SciERC ft_001 在 1 epoch 后 NER F1=0.60）。Few-NERD 训练集大（~66K samples），1 epoch 足以收敛基本模式。Greedy F1=0.78 符合 median 范围 [0.75, 0.85] 的下半段，因为只有 1 epoch。Degeneracy 0.22 在 pilot（200 inst）上初步可见但 CI 宽——这个 pilot 主要验证 pipeline 可行性，不做结论。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Few-NERD Smoke Test Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Training loss (1 epoch)\", \"0.150\"]\n          - [\"Greedy NER F1 (200 inst)\", \"0.780\"]\n          - [\"Oracle NER F1\", \"0.860\"]\n          - [\"Headroom\", \"8.0pp\"]\n          - [\"Parse rate\", \"99.8%\"]\n          - [\"Degeneracy rate (pilot)\", \"22%\"]\n          - [\"SJ ρ (pilot)\", \"0.30\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Training loss curve: single epoch, smooth decrease from ~0.8 to 0.15\"\n    analysis: \"Smoke test PASS。模型成功学会 Few-NERD 格式和 8 类实体标注。Greedy F1=0.78 介于 SciERC（0.66）和 CoNLL（0.91）之间，符合 Few-NERD 的中等难度定位。Degeneracy 初步估计 ~22%，低于 capability trap 线性外推的预测值（~35-40%），暗示 median tier 的'部分确认但不完美拟合'结论。Pipeline validated，proceed to exp-021。\"\n\n  - name: \"fewnerd_full\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: \"Few-NERD 3-epoch LoRA + full test set N=8, 3 seeds. 5 signals + degeneracy + selection.\"\n    expected_results:\n      # Training\n      train_loss_3epoch: 0.065\n      eval_loss_3epoch: 0.078\n      # Core metrics (seed=42 primary, means across 3 seeds in parentheses)\n      greedy_f1: 0.812\n      oracle_f1: 0.895\n      oracle_headroom_pp: 8.3\n      n_test_instances: 1500\n      n_valid_after_gold_filter: 1380\n      parse_rate: 0.999\n      # Degeneracy\n      degeneracy_rate: 0.26\n      degeneracy_rate_3seed_mean: 0.25\n      degeneracy_rate_3seed_sd: 0.018\n      # QE signals (full set, seed=42)\n      sj_rho_full: 0.33\n      fk_rho_full: 0.28\n      logprob_rho_full: 0.25\n      em_rho_full: 0.35\n      voting_conf_rho_full: 0.36\n      sj_auroc_full: 0.72\n      em_auroc_full: 0.78\n      voting_conf_auroc_full: 0.73\n      logprob_auroc_full: 0.68\n      # QE signals (conditional)\n      sj_rho_cond: 0.31\n      em_rho_cond: 0.38\n      voting_conf_rho_cond: 0.33\n      # 3-seed stability\n      sj_rho_3seed_mean: 0.32\n      sj_rho_3seed_sd: 0.025\n      # Selection\n      selection_f1_greedy: 0.812\n      selection_f1_sj: 0.813\n      selection_f1_logprob: 0.814\n      selection_f1_voting_conf: 0.811\n      selection_f1_random: 0.798\n      selection_f1_oracle: 0.895\n      selection_gap_best_minus_greedy_pp: 0.2\n      # Bootstrap on selection gap\n      selection_bootstrap_ci_95_low: -0.8\n      selection_bootstrap_ci_95_high: 1.2\n      selection_permutation_p: 0.42\n      # Capability trap fit\n      capability_trap_f1_vs_degeneracy_r2_with_fewnerd: 0.72\n      capability_trap_monotonicity: true\n      # LP compression\n      lp_within_instance_range_median: 0.038\n      lp_tied_fraction: 0.31\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 6.2\n    result_rationale: \"3-epoch fine-tune 使 greedy F1 从 smoke 的 0.78 提升到 0.812，对应 median 范围 [0.75,0.85] 的中部。Degeneracy rate 0.26 的关键逻辑：capability trap 预测在 F1=0.81 时 degeneracy 应~38%（CoNLL 0.91→58%, SciERC 0.66→21% 的线性外推），但实际只有 26%。原因：(1) Few-NERD 有 8 种实体类型（vs CoNLL 的 4 种），类型多样性提供更多变异维度，使得即使 overall F1 高，individual spans 仍有组合空间；(2) Few-NERD 实例更长/实体更密，per-instance 的 combinatorial space 抑制了完全 convergence。这就是 median 的核心信号：monotonicity 成立（F1 越高 degeneracy 越高），但 R²=0.72 而非 0.95——task structure（类型数、实体密度）是 residual variance 的来源。Selection gap +0.2pp 的逻辑：degeneracy 26% 介于 SciERC（21%，gap≈0）和 CoNLL（58%，gap≈0）之间，bootstrap p=0.42 说明完全不显著。信号排序 VC>EM>SJ>FK>LP 与 CoNLL 类似但 SJ-LP gap 更小（0.08 vs SciERC 的 0.15），因为 8 类系统的 LP 信号比 6 类科学文本更 informative。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Few-NERD Full Results — QE Correlation (ρ, 3-seed mean±sd)\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"NER ρ (full)\", \"NER ρ (cond)\", \"AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Voting_conf\", \"0.360±0.022\", \"0.330±0.028\", \"0.730\"]\n          - [\"EM\", \"0.350±0.019\", \"0.380±0.024\", \"0.780\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.320±0.025\", \"0.310±0.030\", \"0.720\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.280±0.020\", \"0.260±0.025\", \"0.660\"]\n          - [\"Logprob\", \"0.250±0.018\", \"0.220±0.022\", \"0.680\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Few-NERD Selection F1 (N=8, T=1.0)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Δ vs greedy (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Oracle\", \"0.895\", \"+8.3\"]\n          - [\"Logprob\", \"0.814\", \"+0.2\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.813\", \"+0.1\"]\n          - [\"Greedy (T=0)\", \"0.812\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Voting_conf\", \"0.811\", \"-0.1\"]\n          - [\"Random\", \"0.798\", \"-1.4\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Capability Trap — Cross-Dataset Degeneracy\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"Greedy F1\", \"Degeneracy %\", \"Predicted %\", \"Residual\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CoNLL-2003\", \"0.912\", \"58%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Few-NERD\", \"0.812\", \"26%\", \"38%\", \"-12pp\"]\n          - [\"SciERC\", \"0.663\", \"21%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"WNUT-17\", \"0.523\", \"~0%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: F1 vs degeneracy rate (4 datasets). Regression line R²=0.72. Few-NERD sits below the line, indicating task structure modulates the capability-degeneracy relationship.\"\n      - \"Bar chart: Selection F1 across 4 datasets. All signals ≈ greedy on Few-NERD. Error bars (3-seed) overlap heavily.\"\n    analysis: \"Few-NERD 为 capability trap 提供 partial confirmation：degeneracy 单调性成立（F1 越高，degeneracy 越高），但 R² 从 3-point 的 0.95+ 下降到 4-point 的 0.72。这要求将 capability trap 从 'structural inevitability' 调整为 'primary contributing factor'，因为 task structure（类型数量、实体密度）引入了不可忽略的 residual。Selection 结果（+0.2pp, p=0.42）处于 median 定义的模糊区间——不显著优于 greedy，但也没有像 SciERC 那样 greedy 明确 dominate。这使得 'universally fail' 需弱化为 'predominantly fail'。QE signals 仍然有效（SJ ρ=0.32 > LP ρ=0.25），支撑 Claim 2 的 QE framework contribution。\"\n\n  - name: \"3rd_seed_scierc\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: \"SciERC NER+RE N=8, seed=789. 第3个 seed 用于 Fisher combined p-value。\"\n    expected_results:\n      # NER\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.661\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.779\n      ner_headroom_pp: 11.8\n      ner_sj_rho_full: 0.372\n      ner_fk_rho_full: 0.258\n      ner_logprob_rho_full: 0.218\n      ner_em_rho_full: 0.305\n      ner_voting_conf_rho_full: 0.388\n      ner_sj_auroc: 0.698\n      ner_em_auroc: 0.755\n      # RE\n      re_greedy_f1: 0.415\n      re_oracle_f1: 0.582\n      re_headroom_pp: 16.7\n      re_sj_rho_full: 0.258\n      re_fk_rho_full: 0.285\n      re_logprob_rho_full: 0.242\n      re_voting_conf_rho_full: 0.340\n      re_sample_f1_pct_zero: 44.8\n      # RE LP > SJ FLIPS in this seed\n      re_lp_gt_sj: false\n      re_sj_minus_lp_rho: 0.016\n      # 3-seed aggregates (seeds 42, 123/456 existing + 789 new)\n      ner_sj_rho_3seed_mean: 0.381\n      ner_sj_rho_3seed_sd: 0.032\n      re_sj_rho_3seed_mean: 0.261\n      re_sj_rho_3seed_sd: 0.012\n      re_lp_rho_3seed_mean: 0.268\n      re_lp_rho_3seed_sd: 0.038\n      # Fisher combined p-value (SJ > LP on NER, 3 seeds)\n      fisher_combined_p_sj_gt_lp_ner: 0.028\n      fisher_combined_p_sj_gt_lp_ner_significant: true\n      # Fisher combined p-value (LP > SJ on RE, 3 seeds)\n      fisher_combined_p_lp_gt_sj_re: 0.085\n      fisher_combined_p_lp_gt_sj_re_significant: false\n      # Selection\n      selection_f1_greedy: 0.661\n      selection_f1_logprob: 0.654\n      selection_f1_sj: 0.651\n      selection_f1_oracle: 0.779\n      # Degeneracy\n      degeneracy_rate_ner: 0.23\n      n_instances: 529\n      parse_rate: 1.0\n    result_rationale: \"Seed=789 的 NER 结果高度稳定（SJ ρ=0.372 vs 已有 seeds 0.383/0.384/0.360，3-seed SD=0.032 落入 median 范围 [0.02, 0.045]）。关键 median 特征在 RE：seed 789 上 SJ ρ=0.258 略高于 LP ρ=0.242，打破了 seeds 42/123 上 LP>SJ 的 pattern（seed42: LP 0.267 > SJ 0.250; seed123: LP 0.300 > SJ 0.283）。这使得 Fisher combined p for LP>SJ on RE = 0.085（不显著）。翻转原因：RE 的 zero-F1 rate 在不同 seeds 间波动（43-45%），seed=789 恰好有较少的 'complete failure' instances 进入 high-LP bin，削弱了 LP 的 binary classification 优势。NER 上 SJ>LP 的 Fisher p=0.028 仍然显著，支撑 'structural signals dominate for NER' 的结论。但 RE signal ranking 的不稳定性要求将 'LP>SJ for RE' 从 'definitive finding' 降级为 'tendency across most seeds'。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 3-Seed SciERC NER ρ Stability\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"Seed 42\", \"Seed 123\", \"Seed 789\", \"Mean\", \"SD\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.383\", \"0.384\", \"0.372\", \"0.381\", \"0.032\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.259\", \"0.266\", \"0.258\", \"0.261\", \"0.004\"]\n          - [\"LP\", \"0.205\", \"0.226\", \"0.218\", \"0.216\", \"0.011\"]\n          - [\"VC\", \"0.379\", \"0.407\", \"0.388\", \"0.391\", \"0.014\"]\n          - [\"EM\", \"0.295\", \"0.299\", \"0.305\", \"0.300\", \"0.005\"]\n      - name: \"Table: 3-Seed SciERC RE ρ — LP vs SJ Ranking\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"Seed 42\", \"Seed 123\", \"Seed 789\", \"Mean\", \"SD\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LP\", \"0.267\", \"0.300\", \"0.242\", \"0.270\", \"0.029\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.250\", \"0.283\", \"0.258\", \"0.264\", \"0.017\"]\n          - [\"LP>SJ?\", \"Yes (+0.017)\", \"Yes (+0.017)\", \"No (-0.016)\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Fisher Combined p-values (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [\"Hypothesis\", \"Fisher χ²\", \"df\", \"p\", \"Significant?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NER: SJ > LP\", \"14.2\", \"6\", \"0.028\", \"Yes (p<0.05)\"]\n          - [\"RE: LP > SJ\", \"10.8\", \"6\", \"0.085\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: per-seed ρ estimates with 95% bootstrap CI for SJ and LP, NER and RE separately. NER CIs non-overlapping (SJ > LP clear). RE CIs overlapping in seed 789.\"\n    analysis: \"第3个 seed 确认 NER 结论完全稳定（SJ > LP, Fisher p=0.028）。RE 上 LP>SJ 的 ranking 在 seed 789 翻转（SJ 0.258 > LP 0.242），使得 3-seed Fisher p=0.085 未达显著水平。这是 median tier 的核心特征之一：RE signal ranking 不够 robust 以做 definitive claim。Paper 中需表述为 'LP tends to outperform structural signals on RE (2/3 seeds), likely due to binary dominance mechanism, though this advantage does not reach statistical significance across all random seeds (Fisher p=0.085).' Primary claims（capability trap、NER structural>surface、selection fails）在 3-seed 下完全稳定。\"\n\n  - name: \"lora_rank8_ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: \"LoRA rank=8 (vs baseline rank=16) fine-tune on SciERC + N=8 inference. Tests fine-tuning intensity vs capability as degeneracy driver.\"\n    expected_results:\n      # Training\n      train_loss_5epoch: 0.095\n      eval_loss_5epoch: 0.105\n      # Inference — NER\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.641\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.782\n      ner_headroom_pp: 14.1\n      # Degeneracy — KEY METRIC\n      degeneracy_rate_r8: 0.12\n      degeneracy_rate_r16_baseline: 0.21\n      degeneracy_delta_pp: 9.0\n      # QE signals\n      ner_sj_rho_full: 0.365\n      ner_fk_rho_full: 0.270\n      ner_logprob_rho_full: 0.195\n      ner_voting_conf_rho_full: 0.390\n      ner_sj_auroc: 0.690\n      # Selection\n      selection_f1_greedy_r8: 0.641\n      selection_f1_logprob_r8: 0.644\n      selection_f1_sj_r8: 0.642\n      selection_f1_oracle_r8: 0.782\n      selection_gap_logprob_minus_greedy_pp: 0.3\n      # LP compression\n      lp_within_instance_range_median_r8: 0.048\n      lp_tied_fraction_r8: 0.14\n      # RE\n      re_greedy_f1: 0.385\n      re_oracle_f1: 0.568\n      re_degeneracy_rate_r8: 0.08\n      re_sample_f1_pct_zero: 48.2\n      # Comparison with rank=16\n      greedy_f1_delta_r8_minus_r16: -0.022\n      sj_rho_delta_r8_minus_r16: 0.005\n      headroom_delta_r8_minus_r16_pp: 3.0\n      # Non-degenerate selection\n      non_degen_selection_gap_pp: 2.1\n      n_instances: 529\n      parse_rate: 0.995\n    result_rationale: \"LoRA rank=8 的参数容量是 rank=16 的一半，模型 fine-tuning 强度更低。这导致两个效果：(1) greedy F1 略降（0.641 vs 0.663，-2.2pp），因为模型对 SciERC schema 的记忆不如 rank=16 完整；(2) 输出多样性更高，因为 lower-rank adaptation 保留了更多 base model 的 stochastic behavior，degeneracy 从 21% 降到 12%（-9pp，落入 median 范围 [5,15]）。关键逻辑：如果 degeneracy 纯粹由 capability 驱动，则 F1 降低应该已经自动解释 degeneracy 下降（按 capability trap curve：F1 从 0.66 降到 0.64 预测 degeneracy 从 21% 降到 ~19%，仅 -2pp）。但实际下降 9pp >> 2pp 的 capability-predicted 下降，说明 fine-tuning intensity 本身是 independent contributing factor。Median 解读：capability trap 解释了约 22% 的 degeneracy reduction（2/9），fine-tuning intensity 解释了剩余 78%。但 capability 仍是跨 dataset 的 primary driver（CoNLL 58% vs SciERC 21% 的差异远大于 rank ablation 的 9pp）。LP compression 也略微缓解（range median 0.048 vs 0.041），因为 lower fine-tuning 保留了更多 generation-level diversity。Selection 仍不显著（+0.3pp），因为即使 degeneracy 降低，LP compression 仍存在。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LoRA Rank Ablation — Degeneracy & Performance\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Rank=16 (baseline)\", \"Rank=8\", \"Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NER Greedy F1\", \"0.663\", \"0.641\", \"-2.2pp\"]\n          - [\"NER Oracle F1\", \"0.776\", \"0.782\", \"+0.6pp\"]\n          - [\"NER Headroom\", \"11.3pp\", \"14.1pp\", \"+2.8pp\"]\n          - [\"NER Degeneracy %\", \"21%\", \"12%\", \"-9pp\"]\n          - [\"LP range (median nats)\", \"0.041\", \"0.048\", \"+17%\"]\n          - [\"LP tied fraction\", \"0.21\", \"0.14\", \"-7pp\"]\n          - [\"NER SJ ρ\", \"0.383\", \"0.365\", \"-0.018\"]\n          - [\"Best selection F1\", \"0.650 (LP)\", \"0.644 (LP)\", \"-0.6pp\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Degeneracy Attribution (NER)\"\n        columns: [\"Driver\", \"Predicted Δ degen\", \"Actual Δ degen\", \"Attribution %\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Capability (F1 drop 0.66→0.64)\", \"-2pp\", \"—\", \"22%\"]\n          - [\"Fine-tuning intensity (rank 16→8)\", \"—\", \"-7pp\", \"78%\"]\n          - [\"Total observed\", \"—\", \"-9pp\", \"100%\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Non-degenerate Subset Analysis (rank=8)\"\n        columns: [\"Subset\", \"n\", \"LP selection gap\", \"SJ selection gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"All instances\", \"529\", \"+0.3pp\", \"+0.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Non-degenerate only\", \"465\", \"+2.1pp\", \"+1.5pp\"]\n          - [\"Non-degen, rank=16 baseline\", \"418\", \"+2.9pp (p=0.01)\", \"+1.8pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: degeneracy rate by rank (8 vs 16) and dataset (SciERC NER, SciERC RE). Clear reduction at rank=8.\"\n      - \"Scatter: per-instance F1 variance (rank=8 vs rank=16). Rank=8 shows wider spread, especially in mid-F1 range.\"\n    analysis: \"LoRA rank=8 ablation 是 median tier 的 defining experiment。Degeneracy 下降 9pp（从 21% 到 12%）中，capability drop（F1 -2.2pp）仅能解释约 2pp，剩余 7pp 必须归因于 fine-tuning intensity itself。这迫使论文承认 capability trap 不是 sole driver——fine-tuning regime 是 independent contributing factor。但关键上下文是：跨 dataset 的 degeneracy variation（CoNLL 58% vs SciERC 21% = 37pp range）远大于 rank ablation 的 9pp，所以 capability 仍是 'dominant factor'。Paper framing 调整为：'Output convergence is driven by model capability (primary, explaining cross-dataset variance) AND fine-tuning intensity (secondary, contributing 5-15pp within-dataset). The capability trap remains the unifying explanation for why test-time scaling provides diminishing returns as model quality improves.' Selection 仍然 fails 即使 degeneracy 降低，因为 LP compression 是 independent bottleneck（不随 LoRA rank 改变）。\"\n\n  - name: \"claim_audit\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: \"Cross-chapter numerical consistency audit. 检查所有定量 claims vs source data。\"\n    expected_results:\n      contradictions_found: 3\n      contradiction_1:\n        location: \"Discussion vs Limitations\"\n        issue: \"Discussion says '+0.1pp over single-sample', Limitations says '+0.4pp over greedy'\"\n        resolution: \"Both refer to different comparisons: +0.1pp = best signal vs random single, +0.4pp (incorrect) should be +0.6pp = LP vs greedy (from exp_016_rerun_1024). Standardize to LP vs greedy +0.6pp throughout.\"\n      contradiction_2:\n        location: \"Abstract vs Results\"\n        issue: \"Abstract claims 'AUROC up to 0.82' but Results table shows max 0.749 (EM on NER)\"\n        resolution: \"0.82 comes from CoNLL (SJ AUROC=0.8008 in exp_002, EM AUROC=0.8156). Must specify which dataset in Abstract or use max across all: CoNLL EM AUROC 0.82.\"\n      contradiction_3:\n        location: \"Intro vs Section 5\"\n        issue: \"Intro claims '21-58% of instances produce identical F1' — percentages are from 1024-token data but cited numbers use mixed sources\"\n        resolution: \"Verify degeneracy rates from consistent 1024-token runs. SciERC (1024): ~21% (from exp_012_rerun_1024 tied fraction). CoNLL: derive from exp_002 data.\"\n      minor_issues_found: 4\n      total_resolution_time_hours: 2\n    result_rationale: \"Numerical inconsistencies 是 paper 在多轮实验迭代中积累的必然结果。本项目经历了 512→1024 token 数据迁移、gold-empty filtering pipeline 修正、多 seed 数值更新等，每次都有部分 claims 未同步更新。Median tier 假设找到 3 个显著矛盾（realistic for a ~8-page paper with dense quantitative claims）而非 catastrophic level（>5）的问题。这些都是 presentational issues 而非 methodological problems——底层实验数据一致。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Claim Audit Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Issue Type\", \"Count\", \"Severity\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Major numerical contradiction\", \"3\", \"Must fix before submission\"]\n          - [\"Minor rounding/precision inconsistency\", \"4\", \"Fix in final pass\"]\n          - [\"Stale reference to old experiment\", \"2\", \"Update citation\"]\n          - [\"Missing CI/p-value for claimed significance\", \"1\", \"Add from bootstrap data\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Audit 发现 3 个需要修正的矛盾，均为 presentation-level 问题。最关键的是 Discussion/Limitations 中对 selection gap magnitude 的不一致引用——这在 median tier 下尤其敏感，因为 adjusted claims 要求精确措辞（'predominantly fail' 而非 'universally fail'）。所有矛盾均可通过引用正确的 source experiment（exp_012_rerun_1024 为 SciERC 的 canonical source，exp_002 为 CoNLL）解决。无 methodological 问题。建议统一使用 1024-token pipeline 数据作为 paper 中所有 SciERC metrics 的来源。\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56606,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56606},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e9b641f-62a9-4ab0-a8a2-c7358628d967","uuid":"ad497c95-473e-41d8-aeea-d5e815fd2eb8"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":200148,"duration_api_ms":201756,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: \"将 'capability trap' 从 'structural inevitability' 弱化为 'primary contributing factor alongside fine-tuning regime'。两个 failure mechanisms (degeneracy + LP compression) 仍完全成立——它们的证据全部来自已完成实验，不受新实验影响。调整 claims 强度：'universally fail' → 'predominantly fail across tested configurations'。LoRA ablation 变为 nuanced finding：'output convergence is driven by capability AND fine-tuning intensity, with capability as the dominant factor.' 将 QE evaluation framework (Claim 2) 提升为 co-primary contribution。标题微调为 'Strong Predictors, Weak Selectors: Diagnosing Why...' 强调诊断而非绝对性。目标：EMNLP Main（adjusted claims）或 strong Findings。\"\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"fewnerd_smoke\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: \"Few-NERD INTRA coarse 8-type, 1-epoch LoRA fine-tune + 200-instance N=8 pilot. Gate for full run.\"\n    expected_results:\n      train_loss_1epoch: 0.15\n      eval_loss_1epoch: 0.12\n      greedy_f1_200inst: 0.78\n      parse_rate: 0.998\n      pilot_sj_rho_full: 0.30\n      pilot_degeneracy_rate: 0.22\n      pilot_oracle_f1: 0.86\n      pilot_headroom_pp: 8.0\n      inference_time_200inst_minutes: 12\n      n_entity_types: 8\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 8.5\n    result_rationale: \"Few-NERD INTRA coarse（8类通用实体：Person, Organization, Location, Building, Product, Event, Art, Other）比 SciERC 更标准化但比 CoNLL 更细粒度。1-epoch LoRA 已足够让 Qwen3-8B 学会格式和基本类型映射（类似 SciERC ft_001 在 1 epoch 后 NER F1=0.60）。Few-NERD 训练集大（~66K samples），1 epoch 足以收敛基本模式。Greedy F1=0.78 符合 median 范围 [0.75, 0.85] 的下半段，因为只有 1 epoch。Degeneracy 0.22 在 pilot（200 inst）上初步可见但 CI 宽——这个 pilot 主要验证 pipeline 可行性，不做结论。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Few-NERD Smoke Test Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Training loss (1 epoch)\", \"0.150\"]\n          - [\"Greedy NER F1 (200 inst)\", \"0.780\"]\n          - [\"Oracle NER F1\", \"0.860\"]\n          - [\"Headroom\", \"8.0pp\"]\n          - [\"Parse rate\", \"99.8%\"]\n          - [\"Degeneracy rate (pilot)\", \"22%\"]\n          - [\"SJ ρ (pilot)\", \"0.30\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Training loss curve: single epoch, smooth decrease from ~0.8 to 0.15\"\n    analysis: \"Smoke test PASS。模型成功学会 Few-NERD 格式和 8 类实体标注。Greedy F1=0.78 介于 SciERC（0.66）和 CoNLL（0.91）之间，符合 Few-NERD 的中等难度定位。Degeneracy 初步估计 ~22%，低于 capability trap 线性外推的预测值（~35-40%），暗示 median tier 的'部分确认但不完美拟合'结论。Pipeline validated，proceed to exp-021。\"\n\n  - name: \"fewnerd_full\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: \"Few-NERD 3-epoch LoRA + full test set N=8, 3 seeds. 5 signals + degeneracy + selection.\"\n    expected_results:\n      # Training\n      train_loss_3epoch: 0.065\n      eval_loss_3epoch: 0.078\n      # Core metrics (seed=42 primary, means across 3 seeds in parentheses)\n      greedy_f1: 0.812\n      oracle_f1: 0.895\n      oracle_headroom_pp: 8.3\n      n_test_instances: 1500\n      n_valid_after_gold_filter: 1380\n      parse_rate: 0.999\n      # Degeneracy\n      degeneracy_rate: 0.26\n      degeneracy_rate_3seed_mean: 0.25\n      degeneracy_rate_3seed_sd: 0.018\n      # QE signals (full set, seed=42)\n      sj_rho_full: 0.33\n      fk_rho_full: 0.28\n      logprob_rho_full: 0.25\n      em_rho_full: 0.35\n      voting_conf_rho_full: 0.36\n      sj_auroc_full: 0.72\n      em_auroc_full: 0.78\n      voting_conf_auroc_full: 0.73\n      logprob_auroc_full: 0.68\n      # QE signals (conditional)\n      sj_rho_cond: 0.31\n      em_rho_cond: 0.38\n      voting_conf_rho_cond: 0.33\n      # 3-seed stability\n      sj_rho_3seed_mean: 0.32\n      sj_rho_3seed_sd: 0.025\n      # Selection\n      selection_f1_greedy: 0.812\n      selection_f1_sj: 0.813\n      selection_f1_logprob: 0.814\n      selection_f1_voting_conf: 0.811\n      selection_f1_random: 0.798\n      selection_f1_oracle: 0.895\n      selection_gap_best_minus_greedy_pp: 0.2\n      # Bootstrap on selection gap\n      selection_bootstrap_ci_95_low: -0.8\n      selection_bootstrap_ci_95_high: 1.2\n      selection_permutation_p: 0.42\n      # Capability trap fit\n      capability_trap_f1_vs_degeneracy_r2_with_fewnerd: 0.72\n      capability_trap_monotonicity: true\n      # LP compression\n      lp_within_instance_range_median: 0.038\n      lp_tied_fraction: 0.31\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 6.2\n    result_rationale: \"3-epoch fine-tune 使 greedy F1 从 smoke 的 0.78 提升到 0.812，对应 median 范围 [0.75,0.85] 的中部。Degeneracy rate 0.26 的关键逻辑：capability trap 预测在 F1=0.81 时 degeneracy 应~38%（CoNLL 0.91→58%, SciERC 0.66→21% 的线性外推），但实际只有 26%。原因：(1) Few-NERD 有 8 种实体类型（vs CoNLL 的 4 种），类型多样性提供更多变异维度，使得即使 overall F1 高，individual spans 仍有组合空间；(2) Few-NERD 实例更长/实体更密，per-instance 的 combinatorial space 抑制了完全 convergence。这就是 median 的核心信号：monotonicity 成立（F1 越高 degeneracy 越高），但 R²=0.72 而非 0.95——task structure（类型数、实体密度）是 residual variance 的来源。Selection gap +0.2pp 的逻辑：degeneracy 26% 介于 SciERC（21%，gap≈0）和 CoNLL（58%，gap≈0）之间，bootstrap p=0.42 说明完全不显著。信号排序 VC>EM>SJ>FK>LP 与 CoNLL 类似但 SJ-LP gap 更小（0.08 vs SciERC 的 0.15），因为 8 类系统的 LP 信号比 6 类科学文本更 informative。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Few-NERD Full Results — QE Correlation (ρ, 3-seed mean±sd)\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"NER ρ (full)\", \"NER ρ (cond)\", \"AUROC\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Voting_conf\", \"0.360±0.022\", \"0.330±0.028\", \"0.730\"]\n          - [\"EM\", \"0.350±0.019\", \"0.380±0.024\", \"0.780\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.320±0.025\", \"0.310±0.030\", \"0.720\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.280±0.020\", \"0.260±0.025\", \"0.660\"]\n          - [\"Logprob\", \"0.250±0.018\", \"0.220±0.022\", \"0.680\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Few-NERD Selection F1 (N=8, T=1.0)\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"F1\", \"Δ vs greedy (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Oracle\", \"0.895\", \"+8.3\"]\n          - [\"Logprob\", \"0.814\", \"+0.2\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.813\", \"+0.1\"]\n          - [\"Greedy (T=0)\", \"0.812\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Voting_conf\", \"0.811\", \"-0.1\"]\n          - [\"Random\", \"0.798\", \"-1.4\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Capability Trap — Cross-Dataset Degeneracy\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"Greedy F1\", \"Degeneracy %\", \"Predicted %\", \"Residual\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CoNLL-2003\", \"0.912\", \"58%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Few-NERD\", \"0.812\", \"26%\", \"38%\", \"-12pp\"]\n          - [\"SciERC\", \"0.663\", \"21%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"WNUT-17\", \"0.523\", \"~0%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: F1 vs degeneracy rate (4 datasets). Regression line R²=0.72. Few-NERD sits below the line, indicating task structure modulates the capability-degeneracy relationship.\"\n      - \"Bar chart: Selection F1 across 4 datasets. All signals ≈ greedy on Few-NERD. Error bars (3-seed) overlap heavily.\"\n    analysis: \"Few-NERD 为 capability trap 提供 partial confirmation：degeneracy 单调性成立（F1 越高，degeneracy 越高），但 R² 从 3-point 的 0.95+ 下降到 4-point 的 0.72。这要求将 capability trap 从 'structural inevitability' 调整为 'primary contributing factor'，因为 task structure（类型数量、实体密度）引入了不可忽略的 residual。Selection 结果（+0.2pp, p=0.42）处于 median 定义的模糊区间——不显著优于 greedy，但也没有像 SciERC 那样 greedy 明确 dominate。这使得 'universally fail' 需弱化为 'predominantly fail'。QE signals 仍然有效（SJ ρ=0.32 > LP ρ=0.25），支撑 Claim 2 的 QE framework contribution。\"\n\n  - name: \"3rd_seed_scierc\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: \"SciERC NER+RE N=8, seed=789. 第3个 seed 用于 Fisher combined p-value。\"\n    expected_results:\n      # NER\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.661\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.779\n      ner_headroom_pp: 11.8\n      ner_sj_rho_full: 0.372\n      ner_fk_rho_full: 0.258\n      ner_logprob_rho_full: 0.218\n      ner_em_rho_full: 0.305\n      ner_voting_conf_rho_full: 0.388\n      ner_sj_auroc: 0.698\n      ner_em_auroc: 0.755\n      # RE\n      re_greedy_f1: 0.415\n      re_oracle_f1: 0.582\n      re_headroom_pp: 16.7\n      re_sj_rho_full: 0.258\n      re_fk_rho_full: 0.285\n      re_logprob_rho_full: 0.242\n      re_voting_conf_rho_full: 0.340\n      re_sample_f1_pct_zero: 44.8\n      # RE LP > SJ FLIPS in this seed\n      re_lp_gt_sj: false\n      re_sj_minus_lp_rho: 0.016\n      # 3-seed aggregates (seeds 42, 123/456 existing + 789 new)\n      ner_sj_rho_3seed_mean: 0.381\n      ner_sj_rho_3seed_sd: 0.032\n      re_sj_rho_3seed_mean: 0.261\n      re_sj_rho_3seed_sd: 0.012\n      re_lp_rho_3seed_mean: 0.268\n      re_lp_rho_3seed_sd: 0.038\n      # Fisher combined p-value (SJ > LP on NER, 3 seeds)\n      fisher_combined_p_sj_gt_lp_ner: 0.028\n      fisher_combined_p_sj_gt_lp_ner_significant: true\n      # Fisher combined p-value (LP > SJ on RE, 3 seeds)\n      fisher_combined_p_lp_gt_sj_re: 0.085\n      fisher_combined_p_lp_gt_sj_re_significant: false\n      # Selection\n      selection_f1_greedy: 0.661\n      selection_f1_logprob: 0.654\n      selection_f1_sj: 0.651\n      selection_f1_oracle: 0.779\n      # Degeneracy\n      degeneracy_rate_ner: 0.23\n      n_instances: 529\n      parse_rate: 1.0\n    result_rationale: \"Seed=789 的 NER 结果高度稳定（SJ ρ=0.372 vs 已有 seeds 0.383/0.384/0.360，3-seed SD=0.032 落入 median 范围 [0.02, 0.045]）。关键 median 特征在 RE：seed 789 上 SJ ρ=0.258 略高于 LP ρ=0.242，打破了 seeds 42/123 上 LP>SJ 的 pattern（seed42: LP 0.267 > SJ 0.250; seed123: LP 0.300 > SJ 0.283）。这使得 Fisher combined p for LP>SJ on RE = 0.085（不显著）。翻转原因：RE 的 zero-F1 rate 在不同 seeds 间波动（43-45%），seed=789 恰好有较少的 'complete failure' instances 进入 high-LP bin，削弱了 LP 的 binary classification 优势。NER 上 SJ>LP 的 Fisher p=0.028 仍然显著，支撑 'structural signals dominate for NER' 的结论。但 RE signal ranking 的不稳定性要求将 'LP>SJ for RE' 从 'definitive finding' 降级为 'tendency across most seeds'。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 3-Seed SciERC NER ρ Stability\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"Seed 42\", \"Seed 123\", \"Seed 789\", \"Mean\", \"SD\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.383\", \"0.384\", \"0.372\", \"0.381\", \"0.032\"]\n          - [\"FK\", \"0.259\", \"0.266\", \"0.258\", \"0.261\", \"0.004\"]\n          - [\"LP\", \"0.205\", \"0.226\", \"0.218\", \"0.216\", \"0.011\"]\n          - [\"VC\", \"0.379\", \"0.407\", \"0.388\", \"0.391\", \"0.014\"]\n          - [\"EM\", \"0.295\", \"0.299\", \"0.305\", \"0.300\", \"0.005\"]\n      - name: \"Table: 3-Seed SciERC RE ρ — LP vs SJ Ranking\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"Seed 42\", \"Seed 123\", \"Seed 789\", \"Mean\", \"SD\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LP\", \"0.267\", \"0.300\", \"0.242\", \"0.270\", \"0.029\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", \"0.250\", \"0.283\", \"0.258\", \"0.264\", \"0.017\"]\n          - [\"LP>SJ?\", \"Yes (+0.017)\", \"Yes (+0.017)\", \"No (-0.016)\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Fisher Combined p-values (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [\"Hypothesis\", \"Fisher χ²\", \"df\", \"p\", \"Significant?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NER: SJ > LP\", \"14.2\", \"6\", \"0.028\", \"Yes (p<0.05)\"]\n          - [\"RE: LP > SJ\", \"10.8\", \"6\", \"0.085\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: per-seed ρ estimates with 95% bootstrap CI for SJ and LP, NER and RE separately. NER CIs non-overlapping (SJ > LP clear). RE CIs overlapping in seed 789.\"\n    analysis: \"第3个 seed 确认 NER 结论完全稳定（SJ > LP, Fisher p=0.028）。RE 上 LP>SJ 的 ranking 在 seed 789 翻转（SJ 0.258 > LP 0.242），使得 3-seed Fisher p=0.085 未达显著水平。这是 median tier 的核心特征之一：RE signal ranking 不够 robust 以做 definitive claim。Paper 中需表述为 'LP tends to outperform structural signals on RE (2/3 seeds), likely due to binary dominance mechanism, though this advantage does not reach statistical significance across all random seeds (Fisher p=0.085).' Primary claims（capability trap、NER structural>surface、selection fails）在 3-seed 下完全稳定。\"\n\n  - name: \"lora_rank8_ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: \"LoRA rank=8 (vs baseline rank=16) fine-tune on SciERC + N=8 inference. Tests fine-tuning intensity vs capability as degeneracy driver.\"\n    expected_results:\n      # Training\n      train_loss_5epoch: 0.095\n      eval_loss_5epoch: 0.105\n      # Inference — NER\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.641\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.782\n      ner_headroom_pp: 14.1\n      # Degeneracy — KEY METRIC\n      degeneracy_rate_r8: 0.12\n      degeneracy_rate_r16_baseline: 0.21\n      degeneracy_delta_pp: 9.0\n      # QE signals\n      ner_sj_rho_full: 0.365\n      ner_fk_rho_full: 0.270\n      ner_logprob_rho_full: 0.195\n      ner_voting_conf_rho_full: 0.390\n      ner_sj_auroc: 0.690\n      # Selection\n      selection_f1_greedy_r8: 0.641\n      selection_f1_logprob_r8: 0.644\n      selection_f1_sj_r8: 0.642\n      selection_f1_oracle_r8: 0.782\n      selection_gap_logprob_minus_greedy_pp: 0.3\n      # LP compression\n      lp_within_instance_range_median_r8: 0.048\n      lp_tied_fraction_r8: 0.14\n      # RE\n      re_greedy_f1: 0.385\n      re_oracle_f1: 0.568\n      re_degeneracy_rate_r8: 0.08\n      re_sample_f1_pct_zero: 48.2\n      # Comparison with rank=16\n      greedy_f1_delta_r8_minus_r16: -0.022\n      sj_rho_delta_r8_minus_r16: 0.005\n      headroom_delta_r8_minus_r16_pp: 3.0\n      # Non-degenerate selection\n      non_degen_selection_gap_pp: 2.1\n      n_instances: 529\n      parse_rate: 0.995\n    result_rationale: \"LoRA rank=8 的参数容量是 rank=16 的一半，模型 fine-tuning 强度更低。这导致两个效果：(1) greedy F1 略降（0.641 vs 0.663，-2.2pp），因为模型对 SciERC schema 的记忆不如 rank=16 完整；(2) 输出多样性更高，因为 lower-rank adaptation 保留了更多 base model 的 stochastic behavior，degeneracy 从 21% 降到 12%（-9pp，落入 median 范围 [5,15]）。关键逻辑：如果 degeneracy 纯粹由 capability 驱动，则 F1 降低应该已经自动解释 degeneracy 下降（按 capability trap curve：F1 从 0.66 降到 0.64 预测 degeneracy 从 21% 降到 ~19%，仅 -2pp）。但实际下降 9pp >> 2pp 的 capability-predicted 下降，说明 fine-tuning intensity 本身是 independent contributing factor。Median 解读：capability trap 解释了约 22% 的 degeneracy reduction（2/9），fine-tuning intensity 解释了剩余 78%。但 capability 仍是跨 dataset 的 primary driver（CoNLL 58% vs SciERC 21% 的差异远大于 rank ablation 的 9pp）。LP compression 也略微缓解（range median 0.048 vs 0.041），因为 lower fine-tuning 保留了更多 generation-level diversity。Selection 仍不显著（+0.3pp），因为即使 degeneracy 降低，LP compression 仍存在。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LoRA Rank Ablation — Degeneracy & Performance\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Rank=16 (baseline)\", \"Rank=8\", \"Δ\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NER Greedy F1\", \"0.663\", \"0.641\", \"-2.2pp\"]\n          - [\"NER Oracle F1\", \"0.776\", \"0.782\", \"+0.6pp\"]\n          - [\"NER Headroom\", \"11.3pp\", \"14.1pp\", \"+2.8pp\"]\n          - [\"NER Degeneracy %\", \"21%\", \"12%\", \"-9pp\"]\n          - [\"LP range (median nats)\", \"0.041\", \"0.048\", \"+17%\"]\n          - [\"LP tied fraction\", \"0.21\", \"0.14\", \"-7pp\"]\n          - [\"NER SJ ρ\", \"0.383\", \"0.365\", \"-0.018\"]\n          - [\"Best selection F1\", \"0.650 (LP)\", \"0.644 (LP)\", \"-0.6pp\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Degeneracy Attribution (NER)\"\n        columns: [\"Driver\", \"Predicted Δ degen\", \"Actual Δ degen\", \"Attribution %\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Capability (F1 drop 0.66→0.64)\", \"-2pp\", \"—\", \"22%\"]\n          - [\"Fine-tuning intensity (rank 16→8)\", \"—\", \"-7pp\", \"78%\"]\n          - [\"Total observed\", \"—\", \"-9pp\", \"100%\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Non-degenerate Subset Analysis (rank=8)\"\n        columns: [\"Subset\", \"n\", \"LP selection gap\", \"SJ selection gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"All instances\", \"529\", \"+0.3pp\", \"+0.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Non-degenerate only\", \"465\", \"+2.1pp\", \"+1.5pp\"]\n          - [\"Non-degen, rank=16 baseline\", \"418\", \"+2.9pp (p=0.01)\", \"+1.8pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: degeneracy rate by rank (8 vs 16) and dataset (SciERC NER, SciERC RE). Clear reduction at rank=8.\"\n      - \"Scatter: per-instance F1 variance (rank=8 vs rank=16). Rank=8 shows wider spread, especially in mid-F1 range.\"\n    analysis: \"LoRA rank=8 ablation 是 median tier 的 defining experiment。Degeneracy 下降 9pp（从 21% 到 12%）中，capability drop（F1 -2.2pp）仅能解释约 2pp，剩余 7pp 必须归因于 fine-tuning intensity itself。这迫使论文承认 capability trap 不是 sole driver——fine-tuning regime 是 independent contributing factor。但关键上下文是：跨 dataset 的 degeneracy variation（CoNLL 58% vs SciERC 21% = 37pp range）远大于 rank ablation 的 9pp，所以 capability 仍是 'dominant factor'。Paper framing 调整为：'Output convergence is driven by model capability (primary, explaining cross-dataset variance) AND fine-tuning intensity (secondary, contributing 5-15pp within-dataset). The capability trap remains the unifying explanation for why test-time scaling provides diminishing returns as model quality improves.' Selection 仍然 fails 即使 degeneracy 降低，因为 LP compression 是 independent bottleneck（不随 LoRA rank 改变）。\"\n\n  - name: \"claim_audit\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: \"Cross-chapter numerical consistency audit. 检查所有定量 claims vs source data。\"\n    expected_results:\n      contradictions_found: 3\n      contradiction_1:\n        location: \"Discussion vs Limitations\"\n        issue: \"Discussion says '+0.1pp over single-sample', Limitations says '+0.4pp over greedy'\"\n        resolution: \"Both refer to different comparisons: +0.1pp = best signal vs random single, +0.4pp (incorrect) should be +0.6pp = LP vs greedy (from exp_016_rerun_1024). Standardize to LP vs greedy +0.6pp throughout.\"\n      contradiction_2:\n        location: \"Abstract vs Results\"\n        issue: \"Abstract claims 'AUROC up to 0.82' but Results table shows max 0.749 (EM on NER)\"\n        resolution: \"0.82 comes from CoNLL (SJ AUROC=0.8008 in exp_002, EM AUROC=0.8156). Must specify which dataset in Abstract or use max across all: CoNLL EM AUROC 0.82.\"\n      contradiction_3:\n        location: \"Intro vs Section 5\"\n        issue: \"Intro claims '21-58% of instances produce identical F1' — percentages are from 1024-token data but cited numbers use mixed sources\"\n        resolution: \"Verify degeneracy rates from consistent 1024-token runs. SciERC (1024): ~21% (from exp_012_rerun_1024 tied fraction). CoNLL: derive from exp_002 data.\"\n      minor_issues_found: 4\n      total_resolution_time_hours: 2\n    result_rationale: \"Numerical inconsistencies 是 paper 在多轮实验迭代中积累的必然结果。本项目经历了 512→1024 token 数据迁移、gold-empty filtering pipeline 修正、多 seed 数值更新等，每次都有部分 claims 未同步更新。Median tier 假设找到 3 个显著矛盾（realistic for a ~8-page paper with dense quantitative claims）而非 catastrophic level（>5）的问题。这些都是 presentational issues 而非 methodological problems——底层实验数据一致。\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Claim Audit Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Issue Type\", \"Count\", \"Severity\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Major numerical contradiction\", \"3\", \"Must fix before submission\"]\n          - [\"Minor rounding/precision inconsistency\", \"4\", \"Fix in final pass\"]\n          - [\"Stale reference to old experiment\", \"2\", \"Update citation\"]\n          - [\"Missing CI/p-value for claimed significance\", \"1\", \"Add from bootstrap data\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Audit 发现 3 个需要修正的矛盾，均为 presentation-level 问题。最关键的是 Discussion/Limitations 中对 selection gap magnitude 的不一致引用——这在 median tier 下尤其敏感，因为 adjusted claims 要求精确措辞（'predominantly fail' 而非 'universally fail'）。所有矛盾均可通过引用正确的 source experiment（exp_012_rerun_1024 为 SciERC 的 canonical source，exp_002 为 CoNLL）解决。无 methodological 问题。建议统一使用 1024-token pipeline 数据作为 paper 中所有 SciERC metrics 的来源。\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4e9b641f-62a9-4ab0-a8a2-c7358628d967","total_cost_usd":0.657798,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56606,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":9857,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56606,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":9857,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56606},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":51565,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.051655,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":9857,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":56606,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.606143,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"14f0cedd-3ab4-407c-a2f0-9cac2795fd35"}
